    <section class="info-section" id="data-science-section">
      <h5>Data Science Major/Minor</h5>
      <h6>Professors Jumadinova (Chair), Bonham-Carter, Kapfhammer, Luman</h6>
    </br>
      <p2>Data Science focuses on the study of integrated principles and methods to analyze complex big data for decision making, prediction, modeling, and data management. Students examine social and human contexts and ethical implications of how data are collected, analyzed, and utilized in diverse areas.</p2>
    </br>
    </br>
      <h7>Data Science Learning Outcomes</h7>
    </br>
      <ul class="learning-outcomes">
        <li>Effectively collect, organize, analyze, and interpret both structured and unstructured datasets from diverse sources.</li>
        <li>Effectively and ethically use statistical analysis techniques, machine learning algorithms, and software tools to design, build, evaluate, and deploy predictive models.</li>
        <li>Demonstrate and articulate the value of subject matter expertise in domains that apply data science techniques.</li>
        <li>Clearly and persuasively communicate analysis results, including critical reflection on ethical implications.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

